1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,730
One month, jaggery gets costlier.

2
00:00:02,730 --> 00:00:05,179
A new bakery opens near the college.

3
00:00:05,179 --> 00:00:07,866
And everyone starts talking about millets.

4
00:00:08,166 --> 00:00:10,544
None of this happened in Nani's kitchen.

5
00:00:10,544 --> 00:00:12,650
But all of it changes Laddoo Lab.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,384
This is the marketing environment.

7
00:00:15,984 --> 00:00:19,161
Zoya draws Laddoo Lab
in the middle of a page.

8
00:00:19,461 --> 00:00:23,798
Around it, she adds the people and
forces she cannot fully control.

9
00:00:24,398 --> 00:00:26,905
So what is the marketing environment?

10
00:00:27,205 --> 00:00:31,965
Kotler and Armstrong call it the actors
and forces outside marketing that

11
00:00:31,965 --> 00:00:36,543
affect a company's ability to build
relationships with its customers.

12
00:00:36,843 --> 00:00:40,755
Actors are people and groups,
like suppliers and rivals.

13
00:00:40,755 --> 00:00:45,209
Forces are bigger trends, like
prices, laws and new technology.

14
00:00:45,809 --> 00:00:47,769
Inside, Zoya controls a lot.

15
00:00:47,769 --> 00:00:50,868
The recipe, the pack,
the price and the team.

16
00:00:51,168 --> 00:00:53,814
Outside, she controls almost nothing.

17
00:00:53,814 --> 00:00:56,894
Supplier prices, rivals, rules and trends.

18
00:00:57,194 --> 00:01:01,327
So marketers manage what is
inside, and watch what is outside.

19
00:01:01,927 --> 00:01:03,898
You can't control the environment.

20
00:01:03,898 --> 00:01:05,752
But you can be ready for it.

21
00:01:06,452 --> 00:01:10,781
Smart marketers scan the environment,
like a radar, again and again.

22
00:01:11,081 --> 00:01:12,861
First, spot the change.

23
00:01:12,861 --> 00:01:16,126
Jaggery goes from sixty
to eighty rupees a kilo.

24
00:01:16,426 --> 00:01:17,423
Then judge it.

25
00:01:17,423 --> 00:01:19,601
Is it a threat, or an opportunity?

26
00:01:19,601 --> 00:01:21,233
Higher costs are a threat.

27
00:01:21,533 --> 00:01:22,547
Then respond.

28
00:01:22,547 --> 00:01:27,213
Nani now buys jaggery in bulk, straight
from a farmer, so the pack stays

29
00:01:27,213 --> 00:01:28,954
at a hundred and twenty.

30
00:01:29,254 --> 00:01:30,154
Next blip.

31
00:01:30,085 --> 00:01:32,337
The new bakery sells cheap cookies.

32
00:01:32,337 --> 00:01:36,251
Another threat, so Dev shows
parents why laddoos are healthier.

33
00:01:36,551 --> 00:01:41,650
And in 2023, the United Nations marked
the International Year of Millets.

34
00:01:41,650 --> 00:01:42,860
An opportunity!

35
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:45,971
The pack now says, made with ragi millet.

36
00:01:46,571 --> 00:01:48,538
Where do we see this at work today?

37
00:01:48,838 --> 00:01:49,984
Rising costs.

38
00:01:49,984 --> 00:01:54,088
An airline buys fuel in
advance, to protect its fares.

39
00:01:54,388 --> 00:01:55,288
New rivals.

40
00:01:55,283 --> 00:01:58,640
A bank builds a better app
when online banks arrive.

41
00:01:58,940 --> 00:01:59,890
New rules.

42
00:01:59,890 --> 00:02:03,699
A bakery prints allergy
labels when food rules change.

43
00:02:03,999 --> 00:02:04,981
New trends.

44
00:02:04,981 --> 00:02:08,571
A cafe adds plant milk as
more people ask for it.

45
00:02:09,171 --> 00:02:11,519
But can a business always keep up?

46
00:02:11,519 --> 00:02:12,431
Not always.

47
00:02:12,731 --> 00:02:13,918
The good side.

48
00:02:13,918 --> 00:02:17,520
Scanning spots dangers
early, and opens new chances.

49
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:18,975
The hard side.

50
00:02:18,975 --> 00:02:22,390
It takes time, and some
signals are false alarms.

51
00:02:22,690 --> 00:02:26,485
Arjun hears a rumour that
chocolate snacks are the new trend.

52
00:02:26,485 --> 00:02:28,450
He wants to change everything.

53
00:02:28,750 --> 00:02:30,424
Zoya says, check first.

54
00:02:30,424 --> 00:02:33,291
Ask ten parents before
you change the recipe.

55
00:02:33,591 --> 00:02:36,433
And some changes no radar can see.

56
00:02:36,433 --> 00:02:42,140
In March 2020, India's nationwide
lockdown shut most shops almost overnight.

57
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:43,340
The lesson?

58
00:02:43,337 --> 00:02:46,643
Watch the world outside,
and stay ready to change.

59
00:02:47,243 --> 00:02:48,143
Quick check.

60
00:02:48,142 --> 00:02:50,868
A new law bans plastic
film on sweet boxes.

61
00:02:50,868 --> 00:02:53,584
For Laddoo Lab, where does this come from?

62
00:02:55,484 --> 00:02:57,225
The external environment!

63
00:02:57,225 --> 00:03:01,225
It is a force outside the
company that Zoya cannot control.

64
00:03:01,825 --> 00:03:02,838
So, remember.

65
00:03:03,138 --> 00:03:07,622
The marketing environment is the actors
and forces outside marketing that

66
00:03:07,622 --> 00:03:09,196
affect your customers.

67
00:03:09,546 --> 00:03:11,394
You manage what is inside.

68
00:03:11,394 --> 00:03:13,593
Outside, you watch and respond.

69
00:03:13,943 --> 00:03:16,313
Scan, spot, judge and respond.

70
00:03:16,313 --> 00:03:17,609
Again and again.

71
00:03:18,209 --> 00:03:22,636
Next time, we'll explore the
microenvironment and the macroenvironment.
